description: Clean Python for this repo — names, SRP, why-comments, no magic numbers or dumping-ground utils.
globs: "**/*.py"
alwaysApply: false
---
# Clean code

- Names reveal purpose. No `data`, `temp`, `helpers.py`, `misc.py`, `app/utils/` without a real name and two call sites.
- Functions do one thing. Type-hint anything that crosses a layer.
- Comments explain **why**, not syntax. No `print`; structured logs with `notification_id` / `client_id` / `channel`.
- Magic numbers belong in settings (`RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE = 10`, retry countdowns), not literals in tasks.
- `except Exception: pass` is forbidden. Catch the narrowest exception you can handle.
- Leave the file cleaner than you found it; do not mix a reformat of the whole module into a behavior change.
